Relevant columns and how they will be used  
• “boroname”: to isolate the borough (= 'Bronx').  
• “health”: to isolate the desired health category (= 'Good').  
• “tree_id” (or any other non‑NULL column such as “idx”): to count rows (i.e., trees).  

Typical filter conditions  
•  WHERE "boroname" = 'Bronx'  
•  WHERE "health"  = 'Good'  

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑final SQL queries (all SQLite‑compatible) that progressively examine the data and lead to the required percentage calculation.  

```sql
-- 1. Peek at the raw data for sanity
SELECT *
FROM "trees"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. List all borough names recorded in the data set
SELECT DISTINCT "boroname"
FROM "trees"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Count the total number of trees in each borough
SELECT "boroname",
       COUNT(*) AS total_trees
FROM   "trees"
GROUP BY "boroname"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. See all distinct health values in the data
SELECT DISTINCT "health"
FROM "trees"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. How many trees of each health status are in the Bronx?
SELECT "health",
       COUNT(*) AS qty
FROM   "trees"
WHERE  "boroname" = 'Bronx'
GROUP BY "health"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Total number of Bronx trees (for later denominator check)
SELECT COUNT(*) AS total_bronx_trees
FROM   "trees"
WHERE  "boroname" = 'Bronx'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Total number of Bronx trees whose health is Good (for later numerator check)
SELECT COUNT(*) AS good_bronx_trees
FROM   "trees"
WHERE  "boroname" = 'Bronx'
  AND  "health"   = 'Good'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Compute the percentage of Bronx trees that are Good
SELECT ROUND(100.0 *
             SUM(CASE WHEN "health" = 'Good' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) /
             COUNT(*), 2)  -- rounded to two decimals
       AS pct_good_bronx
FROM   "trees"
WHERE  "boroname" = 'Bronx'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. (Extra) Same percentage calculation but for every borough at once
SELECT "boroname",
       ROUND(100.0 *
             SUM(CASE WHEN "health" = 'Good' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) /
             COUNT(*), 2) AS pct_good
FROM   "trees"
GROUP BY "boroname"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Compact version using sub‑queries (numerator / denominator)
SELECT ROUND(100.0 *
            (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM "trees"
              WHERE "boroname" = 'Bronx'
                AND "health"   = 'Good') /
            (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM "trees"
              WHERE "boroname" = 'Bronx'), 2) AS pct_good_bronx;
```
